{
  "$comment": [
    "The apply order for EVERY migration in this repository, across both directories.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (docs/BREEDER_STATE_MODEL.md §9.33). There are two migration",
    "directories and neither is a Supabase CLI root — there is no config.toml in either,",
    "so these are hand-applied SQL files. Two consequences:",
    "",
    "  1. Date prefixes OVERLAP across the directories (20260729 appears in both), so",
    "     'apply in filename order' is ambiguous and there is no tool that resolves it.",
    "  2. Nothing makes a reader aware the second directory exists. That already caused a",
    "     real false finding: §9.5 reported six migrations missing when all six were in",
    "     the root directory, which had never been inspected.",
    "",
    "This file is the answer to both, and `migrationOrder.test.js` asserts it stays",
    "complete — so a migration added to either directory and not listed here FAILS THE",
    "BUILD rather than being silently absent from a fresh-environment bootstrap.",
    "",
    "WHY THE DIRECTORIES WERE NOT MERGED INSTEAD. The filename IS the identity of an",
    "applied migration, and every file here is already applied in production. Renaming or",
    "moving one makes the repo disagree with the record of what was applied, for no",
    "functional gain — the same reasoning as §6.6, which is why widening a CHECK needed a",
    "new file rather than an edit. A manifest fixes the ambiguity without rewriting",
    "history.",
    "",
    "ADDING A MIGRATION: put the file in whichever directory matches its subject (see",
    "`directories` below), then append it here. Order within this list is the order to",
    "apply to a fresh database."
  ],
